From 09481fff2fb736fb44c1390ab4f2168649078c63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:51:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] AI: let an outside chooser make named AI players' build and
 research picks

Off unless FREECIV_HARNESS_DIR and FREECIV_HARNESS_PLAYERS are set. For
the named AI players the default AI asks before it changes a city's
build or the research: it writes question.json in the harness directory
(a status page and up to 8 numbered options, the AI's own pick first),
waits up to FREECIV_HARNESS_TIMEOUT seconds (default 60) for answer.txt
("ID CHOICE"), applies the choice and appends the decision to
applied.jsonl. A timeout or a bad answer keeps the AI's pick.

Between decisions the chooser's pick stays. A city is asked again when
it is new, finishes a build or has its build changed by the game, and
when it is in danger or has been on Coinage for 5 turns, if the AI
would build something else. Research is asked again after each new tech
or when something else changes it. Everything else (units, rates,
government, diplomacy) stays with the AI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
